      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Re will be distributed uniformly within the BCC lattice and will alter the local bonding environment without inducing secondary phases.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Re atoms will segregate to dislocation cores in NbMoTaW.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Re atoms will segregate to irradiation-induced defect sites and act as defect sinks.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "In tungsten alloys, Re reduces the Peierls barrier and activates additional slip systems.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Re-induced reduction of the Peierls barrier and activation of additional slip systems will enhance low-temperature ductility in Re-doped NbMoTaW.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Re will lower defect-mobility barriers and improve irradiation-defect recombination in NbMoTaW.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Re addition will reduce helium-bubble growth and associated blistering in irradiated NbMoTaW.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The Re-doped alloy will show increased room-temperature strain to failure relative to undoped NbMoTaW.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The Re-doped alloy will exhibit less irradiation-induced amorphization, blistering, or precipitation than undoped NbMoTaW.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The high-temperature strength of Re-doped NbMoTaW will remain within approximately 10% of that of undoped NbMoTaW.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
